{
  "id": "spring-microservices-centralized-configuration",
  "slug": "centralized-configuration",
  "title": "Centralized Configuration",
  "category": "Spring Framework",
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "what-is-configuration-in-microservices",
      "heading": "What is Configuration in Microservices?",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Configuration refers to the settings or parameters that microservices need to run properly, such as database connection details, service URLs, credentials, etc."
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 22,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "example-configuration-in-a-microservice-applicationproperties",
          "heading": "Example Configuration in a Microservice (application.properties):",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "",
              "code": "spring.datasource.driverClassName=com.mysql.jdbc.Driver\nspring.datasource.url=jdbc:mysql://localhost/infytel\nspring.datasource.username=root\nspring.datasource.password=root\nspring.jpa.hibernate.ddl-auto=update\nspring.jpa.properties.hibernate.dialect=org.hibernate.dialect.MySQL5Dialect",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 0,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "problem-with-embedded-configuration",
          "heading": "Problem with Embedded Configuration",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "When configuration files are embedded inside each microservice:"
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Any change in configuration requires modifying multiple microservices.",
                "Each microservice must be rebuilt and redeployed after changes.",
                "If a microservice has multiple instances, all instances must be redeployed.",
                "Difficult to maintain consistency across multiple environments (dev, test, prod)."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 46,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "alternatives-for-managing-configuration",
      "heading": "Alternatives for Managing Configuration",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": true,
          "items": [
            "Environment Variables: ",
            "External Files: ",
            "Centralized Configuration Server (Ideal Solution): "
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 9,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "setup-steps-for-spring-cloud-config",
      "heading": "Setup Steps for Spring Cloud Config",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [],
      "wordCount": 0,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "1-create-a-git-repository-for-configuration",
          "heading": "1. Create a Git Repository for Configuration",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Create a repo (e.g., spring-microservice-config) in GitHub or an internal Git server.",
                "Add common properties in a file called application.properties:"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "",
              "code": "spring.datasource.driverClassName=com.mysql.jdbc.Driver\nspring.jpa.hibernate.ddl-auto=update\nspring.jpa.properties.hibernate.dialect=org.hibernate.dialect.MySQL5Dialect",
              "runnable": false
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Create individual property files for each microservice named exactly as their spring.application.name, e.g., customer-service.properties or order-service.properties."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 36,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "2-create-config-server-project",
          "heading": "2. Create Config Server Project",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Create a Spring Boot project with Spring Cloud Config Server dependency:"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "xml",
              "code": "<dependencyManagement>\n  <dependencies>\n    <dependency>\n      <groupId>org.springframework.cloud</groupId>\n      <artifactId>spring-cloud-dependencies</artifactId>\n      <version>Greenwich.RELEASE</version>\n      <type>pom</type>\n      <scope>import</scope>\n    </dependency>\n  </dependencies>\n</dependencyManagement>\n\n<dependency>\n  <groupId>org.springframework.cloud</groupId>\n  <artifactId>spring-cloud-config-server</artifactId>\n</dependency>",
              "runnable": false
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Configure Git repo URL in application.properties or application.yml of config server:"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "",
              "code": "server.port=1111\nspring.application.name=config-server\nspring.cloud.config.server.git.uri=https://github.com/yourorg/spring-microservice-config.git",
              "runnable": false
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Enable Config Server by adding annotation in main application class:"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "java",
              "code": "@EnableConfigServer\n@SpringBootApplication\npublic class ConfigServerApplication { ... }",
              "runnable": false
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 32,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "3-configure-microservices-as-config-clients",
          "heading": "3. Configure Microservices as Config Clients",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Add Spring Cloud Config Client dependency:"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "xml",
              "code": "<dependencyManagement>\n  <dependencies>\n    <dependency>\n      <groupId>org.springframework.cloud</groupId>\n      <artifactId>spring-cloud-dependencies</artifactId>\n      <version>Greenwich.RELEASE</version>\n      <type>pom</type>\n      <scope>import</scope>\n    </dependency>\n  </dependencies>\n</dependencyManagement>\n\n<dependency>\n  <groupId>org.springframework.cloud</groupId>\n  <artifactId>spring-cloud-starter-config</artifactId>\n</dependency>",
              "runnable": false
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Create a bootstrap.properties (or application.properties for Spring Boot >2.4.x) in each microservice specifying the config server URL:"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "",
              "code": "spring.cloud.config.uri=http://localhost:1111\nspring.datasource.username=root\nspring.datasource.password=root",
              "runnable": false
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Remove sensitive details from microservice’s application.properties."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 29,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "how-configurations-are-loaded",
          "heading": "How Configurations are Loaded",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Spring Cloud creates a bootstrap context (parent to application context) responsible for loading external configuration from Config Server.",
                "Properties from Config Server take higher precedence over local properties.",
                "bootstrap.properties or the new spring.config.import property is used to point microservices to the config server."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 43,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "configuration-file-naming-and-profiles",
      "heading": "Configuration File Naming and Profiles",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "The config server looks for config files named after the client’s spring.application.name.",
            "Multiple profiles can be supported, for example: customer-service-dev.properties\ncustomer-service-prod.properties",
            "Load order for configuration files: ",
            "Properties in higher priority files override lower priority ones."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 35,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "runtime-behavior-and-refreshing-configuration",
      "heading": "Runtime Behavior and Refreshing Configuration",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Config clients fetch configuration only once at startup.",
            "Changes made in Git after startup are not reflected automatically.",
            "To update configurations dynamically:  <dependency>\n    <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n    <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-actuator</artifactId>\n</dependency>  management.endpoints.web.exposure.include=*  curl -X POST http://localhost:8001/actuator/refresh",
            "If you access properties directly via Environment.getProperty(), you do not need @RefreshScope."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 43,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "handling-multiple-microservices-and-refresh-events",
          "heading": "Handling Multiple Microservices and Refresh Events",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Manually triggering /refresh on every microservice is tedious for large systems.",
                "Spring Cloud Bus (with messaging middleware like RabbitMQ) can broadcast refresh events automatically to all microservices.",
                "Spring Cloud Bus is beyond basic scope but important for real-world systems."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 39,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "additional-notes",
      "heading": "Additional Notes",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "If the config server is down, microservices fallback to their local configuration.",
            "To fail fast on config server failures, use: spring.cloud.config.failFast=true",
            "Config server default port: 8888",
            "Config server can be scaled horizontally for high availability.",
            "Use Personal Access Tokens for Git authentication instead of passwords for better security.",
            "From Spring Boot 2.4+, bootstrap.properties is deprecated; instead, use: spring.config.import=optional:configserver:http://localhost:1111"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 58,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "summary",
      "heading": "Summary",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Concept",
            "Explanation"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Centralized Config Server",
              "Single place to store microservices configuration using Git and Spring Cloud Config Server"
            ],
            [
              "Bootstrap Context",
              "Loads external configs with higher precedence before application context"
            ],
            [
              "Config Client Setup",
              "Microservices configured to fetch configs from Config Server at startup"
            ],
            [
              "Refreshing Configs",
              "Use @RefreshScope and actuator /refresh endpoint for runtime config update"
            ],
            [
              "Profiles Support",
              "Supports multiple environments with profile-specific property files"
            ],
            [
              "Fail Fast",
              "Option to fail at startup if Config Server unreachable"
            ],
            [
              "Security",
              "Use tokens for Git authentication, secure config server connections"
            ],
            [
              "Cloud-native Approach",
              "Externalized configuration supports dynamic scaling and agility in cloud environments"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 96,
      "subsections": []
    }
  ],
